# Cloudflare Workers static-asset redirects. 2,000 static rules allowed.
#
# This file is the reason the site is on Cloudflare rather than GitHub Pages:
# Pages cannot issue a real 301, only an HTML meta-refresh, which passes link
# equity poorly and shows the reader a flash of the wrong page.
#
# NOTE: _redirects cannot match on hostname. The old GitHub Pages host is
# consolidated by a redirect stub published to that host — see
# .github/workflows/legacy-pages-redirect.yml.
#
# No rules yet. html_handling: "drop-trailing-slash" in wrangler.jsonc already
# 307s /docs/typeorm/ -> /docs/typeorm, so trailing-slash variants need no lines
# here. Add a 301 whenever a page is merged into another or moves URL.
